WEBVTT

00:00:06.270 --> 00:00:07.670
15-love.

00:00:07.670 --> 00:00:12.060
Wow, Egawa-kun's serves 
never fail to mesmerize me!

00:00:12.060 --> 00:00:15.210
In terms of speed alone, 
he might be number one in Japan.

00:00:15.210 --> 00:00:19.820
There aren't many Japanese who have a
physique like his and can move like that.

00:00:20.390 --> 00:00:25.540
Yes, he may be the one to follow 
Ike Soji in taking on the world.

00:00:25.540 --> 00:00:27.330
Right, Miura-san?

00:00:27.330 --> 00:00:30.050
He must be starting to take on 
a professional mindset, too.

00:00:30.260 --> 00:00:33.000
I can't wait to see Bro show 
the results of his hard work

00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:36.200
and find out how well he can 
hold out against Takuma-san!

00:00:36.900 --> 00:00:37.670
Yeah.

00:02:09.410 --> 00:02:13.400
Moonlight and the Sound of Waves

00:02:14.650 --> 00:02:17.840
First set winner: Egawa. 6-2.

00:02:19.060 --> 00:02:23.660
<i>The quality of Takuma-san's serve is 
totally different from a few months ago.</i>

00:02:24.360 --> 00:02:27.330
<i>It stretches away from my reach after
the bounce, just like Ike-kun's.</i>

00:02:27.670 --> 00:02:29.460
<i>But it's not something I can't return.</i>

00:02:30.070 --> 00:02:33.670
<i>If I change the pace so I don't 
give him a chance to move up...</i>

00:02:34.490 --> 00:02:38.380
Bro hasn't given up at all against Takuma-san.

00:02:38.380 --> 00:02:39.430
Yeah.

00:02:40.140 --> 00:02:40.930
Okay!

00:02:41.170 --> 00:02:42.580
Second set.

00:02:45.720 --> 00:02:47.430
<i>I'm gonna be aggressive!</i>

00:02:51.850 --> 00:02:54.230
<i>Before he can grasp the 
timing of my topspin shots,</i>

00:02:54.230 --> 00:02:55.360
<i>use a slice!</i>

00:02:56.120 --> 00:02:59.860
<i>Change the pace from a high-arcing topspin 
to a slice that stays in the air longer</i>

00:02:59.860 --> 00:03:01.460
<i>and doesn't bounce high.</i>

00:03:02.030 --> 00:03:04.710
<i>And when his speed drops to match my timing,</i>

00:03:04.710 --> 00:03:06.540
<i>waste no time striking with a flat shot!</i>

00:03:08.180 --> 00:03:09.370
Love-15.

00:03:09.370 --> 00:03:10.480
Yes!

00:03:12.050 --> 00:03:13.800
He's looking good out there!

00:03:13.800 --> 00:03:14.630
Yeah!

00:03:14.630 --> 00:03:18.140
Maruo-kun is doing a fine 
job of changing the pace!

00:03:18.140 --> 00:03:20.380
He's hitting a variety of shots.

00:03:20.640 --> 00:03:22.240
<i>Return his shots!</i>

00:03:22.240 --> 00:03:24.890
<i>What I lack in power, 
I can make up for in control.</i>

00:03:30.010 --> 00:03:33.810
He's made remarkable improvements 
since I last saw him.

00:03:34.760 --> 00:03:36.900
Has he been a member of STC for long?

00:03:37.180 --> 00:03:39.700
No, he's been playing for only two years.

00:03:39.700 --> 00:03:41.680
He's our most promising player.

00:03:41.680 --> 00:03:42.810
Only two years?

00:03:43.240 --> 00:03:44.000
Yes.

00:03:44.470 --> 00:03:46.410
I never knew that.

00:03:46.720 --> 00:03:48.060
<i>That's right.</i>

00:03:48.060 --> 00:03:50.410
<i>I've known Ei-chan for two years now.</i>

00:03:52.290 --> 00:03:53.880
Incredible.

00:03:53.880 --> 00:03:56.420
Not only is he returning Egawa-kun's shots,

00:03:56.420 --> 00:03:58.300
but he's actually going for points.

00:03:58.650 --> 00:04:02.050
He has a surprising variety of 
shots and amazing accuracy.

00:04:02.050 --> 00:04:05.220
He may be good enough to 
write an article about soon.

00:04:06.470 --> 00:04:07.440
That's true!

00:04:10.580 --> 00:04:11.310
Yes!

00:04:12.310 --> 00:04:14.810
Game: Maruo. 3-all.

00:04:17.560 --> 00:04:18.570
<i>Now!</i>

00:04:23.380 --> 00:04:24.200
Yeah!

00:04:24.200 --> 00:04:26.070
Game: Maruo. 4-all.

00:04:26.070 --> 00:04:27.200
Wow!

00:04:31.800 --> 00:04:33.860
Game: Egawa. 5-4.

00:04:33.860 --> 00:04:35.940
<i>Takuma-san is incredible.</i>

00:04:35.940 --> 00:04:38.210
<i>It's all I can do just to hold serve!</i>

00:04:38.210 --> 00:04:40.260
Wow, they're on fire!

00:04:38.210 --> 00:04:43.170
Egawa 
Maruo

00:04:40.260 --> 00:04:43.170
If Egawa-kun can break serve now, he'll win.

00:04:46.180 --> 00:04:48.680
<i>Get the timing right again 
for another flat shot!</i>

00:04:50.680 --> 00:04:51.360
Yeah!

00:04:51.360 --> 00:04:53.290
Game: Maruo. 5-all.

00:04:56.190 --> 00:04:57.570
Ei-chan's amazing!

00:04:56.190 --> 00:04:58.690
Egawa 
Maruo

00:04:57.570 --> 00:04:58.690
He did it!

00:05:09.910 --> 00:05:12.840
Bro's really getting into 
his game with Takuma-san.

00:05:12.840 --> 00:05:14.580
<i>Keep it up, Ei-chan!</i>

00:05:18.640 --> 00:05:20.140
Game, set, and match.

00:05:20.140 --> 00:05:21.340
Winner: Egawa.

00:05:21.340 --> 00:05:24.120
Score: 6-2, 7-5.

00:05:21.340 --> 00:05:24.840
Egawa 
Maruo

00:05:25.250 --> 00:05:29.350
<i>I was right to use my data from 
the first set in the second set.</i>

00:05:29.770 --> 00:05:32.880
<i>But there's still a bigger difference 
in strength than the scores show.</i>

00:05:36.320 --> 00:05:38.140
You've gotten a lot better.

00:05:39.290 --> 00:05:40.490
Thanks!

00:05:44.110 --> 00:05:47.610
Takuma-san! That was a pretty intense match!

00:05:50.620 --> 00:05:53.560
<i>One week remains until the Kanto Junior.</i>

00:05:53.560 --> 00:05:55.110
<i>I need to focus!</i>

00:05:58.550 --> 00:05:59.880
Yes!

00:06:03.370 --> 00:06:07.700
Maruo-kun, you're able to hit the 
ball right where it hurts now.

00:06:08.180 --> 00:06:09.440
Thanks!

00:06:09.440 --> 00:06:10.430
Maruo-kun.

00:06:11.310 --> 00:06:12.640
What's up, Iwasa-kun?

00:06:12.890 --> 00:06:15.540
I just realized something 
as I was sketching you.

00:06:15.540 --> 00:06:18.730
You're hitting all your forehand 
shots with the same form.

00:06:18.730 --> 00:06:19.780
Really?

00:06:19.780 --> 00:06:20.880
Also, these are great!

00:06:20.880 --> 00:06:22.350
They look just like you!

00:06:22.350 --> 00:06:23.140
Yeah!

00:06:23.800 --> 00:06:26.530
<i>We're in an adjustment period 
focusing on pratice matches,</i>

00:06:26.530 --> 00:06:28.740
<i>but with Miyagawa-kun and 
Iwasa-kun joining us,</i>

00:06:28.740 --> 00:06:30.660
<i>it's been a very fulfilling experience.</i>

00:06:32.600 --> 00:06:35.460
Knowing you, I'm certain you won't forget,

00:06:35.460 --> 00:06:39.000
but be sure to keep your 
first round opponent in mind.

00:06:39.000 --> 00:06:40.170
Right!

00:06:42.890 --> 00:06:44.630
Here it is.

00:06:44.630 --> 00:06:48.170
This is a video of your first round opponent.

00:06:49.010 --> 00:06:50.680
<i>Yakabe to serve.</i>

00:06:51.210 --> 00:06:52.600
Yakabe Tadanori.

00:06:52.600 --> 00:06:54.330
He made top eight at the Tokyo Junior,

00:06:54.330 --> 00:06:56.620
and he's number 36 in the Kanto Junior ranking

00:06:56.620 --> 00:06:58.260
as a third-year in high school.

00:06:58.260 --> 00:06:59.040
Okay.

00:06:59.040 --> 00:07:01.340
I think we also have video of Ide,

00:07:01.340 --> 00:07:03.630
the guy you're likely to 
face in the second round,

00:07:03.630 --> 00:07:06.620
but you've seen him in 
person a few times, right?

00:07:06.620 --> 00:07:09.670
Yeah, but I'll still watch what we have.

00:07:10.270 --> 00:07:13.200
It's better to have as much data 
on my opponents as possible.

00:07:13.200 --> 00:07:15.770
Okay, I'm gonna get back to practice.

00:07:15.770 --> 00:07:17.280
Thanks, Yukichi-kun.

00:07:19.710 --> 00:07:21.520
<i>Ide Yoshiaki.</i>

00:07:21.520 --> 00:07:25.360
<i>He made the top eight at the All-Japan 
Junior Indoor Invitational,</i>

00:07:25.360 --> 00:07:27.710
<i>but at the Saitama Junior, 
he lost in the top eight.</i>

00:07:29.100 --> 00:07:29.970
<i>Double fault.</i>

00:07:30.800 --> 00:07:32.290
<i>Advantage: Chiba.</i>

00:07:33.240 --> 00:07:36.760
<i>A power shot on the second serve got him a
double fault at deuce with the score 5-5?</i>

00:07:37.070 --> 00:07:40.730
<i>I can't believe he'd take a risk 
that huge at such a crucial moment.</i>

00:07:43.560 --> 00:07:44.620
<i>Yes!</i>

00:07:44.620 --> 00:07:45.230
<i>Deuce!</i>

00:07:45.230 --> 00:07:48.690
<i>But that high confidence is proving effective.</i>

00:07:49.140 --> 00:07:53.180
<i>It's fun to watch players who aren't afraid 
of missing, which hypes up the crowd.</i>

00:07:53.180 --> 00:07:55.790
<i>Then Ide-kun gets just as hyped up,</i>

00:07:55.790 --> 00:07:58.550
<i>and the synergistic effect makes 
him play better and better.</i>

00:07:58.550 --> 00:08:04.000
<i>That allows him to win all 
the high-pressure points.</i>

00:08:04.310 --> 00:08:06.930
<i>Game: Ide. 6-5.</i>

00:08:04.630 --> 00:08:08.000
<i>He's a type of player I've never faced before.</i>

00:08:11.560 --> 00:08:14.760
All right! It's summer break... Ah...

00:08:15.350 --> 00:08:18.660
Are you two going to spend your 
whole break playing tennis again?

00:08:18.660 --> 00:08:20.460
Yep, that's right.

00:08:20.460 --> 00:08:22.270
The Kanto Junior's coming up.

00:08:22.270 --> 00:08:24.770
Is that an important match?

00:08:24.770 --> 00:08:28.810
Yeah. Players who finish in the top sixteen

00:08:28.810 --> 00:08:31.850
get to participate in the 
All-Japan Junior in mid-August.

00:08:31.850 --> 00:08:34.780
It's the tournament that determines
the best high school player in Japan.

00:08:34.780 --> 00:08:38.830
Wow! I had no idea you had 
both reached that stage!

00:08:38.830 --> 00:08:40.790
That's only if we win, though.

00:08:41.410 --> 00:08:44.880
<i>Didn't Ei-chan say if he 
doesn't win that tournament,</i>

00:08:44.880 --> 00:08:47.020
<i>he has to give up on going pro?</i>

00:08:47.930 --> 00:08:49.290
I'll come cheer you on!

00:08:50.970 --> 00:08:52.090
I will, too!

00:08:52.090 --> 00:08:53.270
Thanks!

00:08:53.270 --> 00:08:54.970
Let's do our best, Ei-chan!

00:08:54.970 --> 00:08:55.800
Yep!

00:08:59.380 --> 00:09:02.040
It's almost time for that 
tennis tournament, isn't it?

00:09:02.040 --> 00:09:03.400
Oh... Yeah.

00:09:03.400 --> 00:09:07.400
You'll have to make a lot of 
decisions over this summer break.

00:09:08.070 --> 00:09:11.560
Are you really going to give up 
on the pros if you don't win?

00:09:13.190 --> 00:09:14.400
I intend to.

00:09:14.740 --> 00:09:17.170
Well, do your very best.

00:09:17.170 --> 00:09:18.410
We're rooting for you.

00:09:18.920 --> 00:09:19.590
Okay.

00:09:20.680 --> 00:09:22.000
<i>I have to win!</i>

00:09:22.540 --> 00:09:24.010
<i>I'll win and go pro!</i>

00:09:33.390 --> 00:09:35.380
Everyone got your stuff loaded?

00:09:35.380 --> 00:09:36.420
Yes!

00:09:36.420 --> 00:09:37.930
All right, let's go.

00:09:43.730 --> 00:09:45.430
Sure is a lot of traffic.

00:09:45.430 --> 00:09:46.840
Y-Yeah...

00:09:47.620 --> 00:09:49.490
Are you getting carsick?

00:09:49.490 --> 00:09:50.950
Oh, nah.

00:09:50.950 --> 00:09:54.260
It's my first time staying 
overnight for a tennis match,

00:09:54.260 --> 00:09:55.700
so I'm just a little nervous.

00:09:55.700 --> 00:09:56.460
Huh?

00:09:56.460 --> 00:09:58.860
We're only going to Chiba.

00:09:58.860 --> 00:10:01.950
You went to Florida. 
What are you so worked up about?

00:10:02.320 --> 00:10:06.180
Master Ike and Takuma-san 
travel all over the world!

00:10:06.650 --> 00:10:09.610
Once you go pro, you'll be traveling a lot more,

00:10:09.610 --> 00:10:11.450
so you'd better get used to it!

00:10:11.450 --> 00:10:13.740
Getting over being ruled by your 
surroundings isn't enough.

00:10:13.740 --> 00:10:16.890
You've gotta be able to use 
them to your advantage.

00:10:16.890 --> 00:10:20.470
Anyway, isn't this fun? It's like a vacation.

00:10:17.570 --> 00:10:21.160
The car in front of us is moving! Eyes front!

00:10:21.160 --> 00:10:22.970
You'll be fine, Ei-chan.

00:10:23.220 --> 00:10:23.950
Huh?

00:10:23.950 --> 00:10:26.210
Florida was your first trip overseas,

00:10:26.210 --> 00:10:28.650
but you came back looking totally comfortable.

00:10:28.650 --> 00:10:31.420
I worried about you all that time for nothing.

00:10:31.420 --> 00:10:34.220
True, as attuned to detail as you are,

00:10:34.220 --> 00:10:36.850
you can be pretty dense about things, Bro.

00:10:36.850 --> 00:10:39.030
A-Am I?

00:10:39.030 --> 00:10:39.990
Yep, you are.

00:10:40.200 --> 00:10:41.530
You're actually pretty slow!

00:10:41.530 --> 00:10:43.200
I am not!

00:10:45.700 --> 00:10:47.950
Welcome

00:10:45.700 --> 00:10:47.950
Ayano TC   STC   Seishiro Academy

00:10:48.460 --> 00:10:50.710
Thanks for having us.

00:10:50.710 --> 00:10:51.980
All right,

00:10:51.980 --> 00:10:55.640
for today, you'll spend the next two 
hours working up a sweat on the courts.

00:10:55.640 --> 00:10:58.390
Make sure to get plenty of carbs at dinner,

00:10:58.390 --> 00:11:00.220
and get to bed as early as you can.

00:11:00.710 --> 00:11:05.180
Tomorrow, be sure to finish breakfast at 
least three hours before your match begins,

00:11:05.180 --> 00:11:08.730
and warm up thoroughly before your match.

00:11:08.730 --> 00:11:12.470
And those who lose will immediately 
hop on a train back home.

00:11:13.410 --> 00:11:14.230
That is all.

00:11:14.230 --> 00:11:17.980
Hey, you're our coach! 
Don't say ominous things like that!

00:11:18.370 --> 00:11:20.390
That part is different from a vacation.

00:11:20.390 --> 00:11:21.500
Huh?!

00:11:21.500 --> 00:11:23.170
How can you make such casual remarks?!

00:11:23.170 --> 00:11:24.740
This is about survival!

00:11:24.970 --> 00:11:25.810
That's right.

00:11:25.810 --> 00:11:28.780
Isn't that kinda cool? It's like a game.

00:11:28.780 --> 00:11:31.750
Okay, drop off your stuff in your 
rooms, then meet in the lobby.

00:11:34.790 --> 00:11:37.750
We'll be staying here for up to seven days.

00:11:38.700 --> 00:11:41.260
There's a laundromat on the first floor.

00:11:41.260 --> 00:11:44.260
Kanto Junior Tennis Tournament

00:11:44.910 --> 00:11:46.260
So hot...

00:11:46.570 --> 00:11:48.520
<i>There are so many people here already.</i>

00:11:49.030 --> 00:11:51.020
<i>So this is the venue for tomorrow's matches.</i>

00:11:55.870 --> 00:11:57.470
Nabae-kun's here!

00:11:57.470 --> 00:11:58.650
Yo!

00:11:59.240 --> 00:12:00.270
Araya-kun!

00:12:00.270 --> 00:12:01.780
How're you feeling?

00:12:02.000 --> 00:12:04.780
It's hot, so don't wear yourself out practicing.

00:12:05.000 --> 00:12:06.550
Let's play a round later!

00:12:06.550 --> 00:12:07.280
Sure!

00:12:08.810 --> 00:12:11.440
Bro, let's warm up.

00:12:11.440 --> 00:12:12.290
Okay.

00:12:22.510 --> 00:12:24.350
This is great.

00:12:24.350 --> 00:12:25.940
Wash off all your fatigue!

00:12:25.940 --> 00:12:26.760
Yeah.

00:12:26.760 --> 00:12:29.470
Nothing beats a bath after practice!

00:12:29.470 --> 00:12:31.020
Yeah, it feels great.

00:12:31.300 --> 00:12:33.090
Aren't tours like these fun?

00:12:33.090 --> 00:12:34.600
How's it going for you?

00:12:34.600 --> 00:12:36.260
Yeah, it's fun.

00:12:36.980 --> 00:12:40.040
Actually, when I think we have 
matches starting tomorrow,

00:12:40.040 --> 00:12:42.660
I have to wonder whether we
should be having this much fun.

00:12:42.660 --> 00:12:45.030
That's the problem with you newbies.

00:12:45.030 --> 00:12:49.130
Listen. On tours, you have fun 
when you're meant to have fun,

00:12:49.130 --> 00:12:51.790
and work hard when you need to work hard.

00:12:51.790 --> 00:12:53.150
I see...

00:12:53.150 --> 00:12:55.290
Start by just relaxing.

00:12:55.290 --> 00:12:56.180
Okay.

00:12:56.180 --> 00:12:58.070
It's like a school field trip, isn't it?

00:12:58.070 --> 00:12:59.290
Yeah, it is.

00:13:01.090 --> 00:13:04.050
Okay, I'll call you again tomorrow.

00:13:05.590 --> 00:13:06.300
Yeah.

00:13:07.140 --> 00:13:08.870
Yeah, I know.

00:13:08.870 --> 00:13:10.310
I know, I know!

00:13:10.310 --> 00:13:11.160
Okay, bye.

00:13:18.170 --> 00:13:20.320
Oh, Ei-chan. What's up?

00:13:20.620 --> 00:13:23.450
I was just calling home. What about you?

00:13:23.450 --> 00:13:25.320
I came to get a drink.

00:13:26.000 --> 00:13:28.020
So it finally starts tomorrow.

00:13:28.020 --> 00:13:31.340
Yeah. For the past year, I've trained for this...

00:13:31.340 --> 00:13:34.330
No, I've trained for the All-Japan Junior,

00:13:34.330 --> 00:13:36.140
so there's a lot on my mind.

00:13:38.830 --> 00:13:39.940
Oh, yeah!

00:13:39.940 --> 00:13:41.760
Ei-chan, come with me for a bit.

00:13:44.370 --> 00:13:46.340
I'll show you something really cool.

00:13:46.610 --> 00:13:48.770
Huh? Where are we going?

00:13:48.770 --> 00:13:51.990
If we're going out, shouldn't 
we let the coach know?

00:13:51.990 --> 00:13:53.350
It'll be fine.

00:13:54.640 --> 00:13:56.350
This isn't school.

00:13:56.350 --> 00:13:58.350
Oh, you're right.

00:13:58.590 --> 00:14:00.760
Or do you not want to see something cool?

00:14:00.760 --> 00:14:03.360
N-No, I do! I want to see it!

00:14:05.590 --> 00:14:07.090
Then let's go.

00:14:07.090 --> 00:14:10.010
It's really close. We'll be fine.

00:14:10.010 --> 00:14:10.920
Okay.

00:14:13.470 --> 00:14:15.000
So what's this cool thing?

00:14:15.270 --> 00:14:17.030
You'll find out soon.

00:14:17.030 --> 00:14:20.750
By the way, what were you planning 
to do for the rest of tonight?

00:14:20.750 --> 00:14:24.250
Huh? Well, I hadn't really thought about it.

00:14:24.810 --> 00:14:28.760
I'll probably go over my notes and 
stuff to prepare for tomorrow.

00:14:29.540 --> 00:14:32.510
But you don't feel like there's 
anything left you could do?

00:14:32.510 --> 00:14:36.730
Well, sure, but I can't fall 
asleep at 8:00 in the evening,

00:14:36.730 --> 00:14:40.520
and I wouldn't feel ready for my 
match tomorrow if I did nothing.

00:14:40.520 --> 00:14:43.360
Yeah, I know what you mean.

00:14:43.360 --> 00:14:46.260
I talked to Aoi-san about that not long ago.

00:14:46.260 --> 00:14:48.930
He said that once you go pro 
and start touring more,

00:14:48.930 --> 00:14:54.030
the ability to use your extra time 
wisely becomes really important.

00:14:54.030 --> 00:14:56.610
The ability to use time wisely?

00:14:56.610 --> 00:15:01.010
It's not good to have too much running 
through your head before a match, right?

00:15:01.010 --> 00:15:03.040
But you can't just think about nothing, either.

00:15:03.880 --> 00:15:10.880
He said you should learn how to relax in 
your own way while continuing to focus.

00:15:10.880 --> 00:15:11.800
Oh...

00:15:11.800 --> 00:15:18.910
Tennis 60

00:15:11.800 --> 00:15:23.310
College Entrance Exam  
English Vocabulary

00:15:12.230 --> 00:15:14.680
I think I sort of understand.

00:15:14.680 --> 00:15:18.360
I can't just spend the rest of 
the day looking at my notes,

00:15:18.360 --> 00:15:23.310
so I was thinking of going running or 
borrowing a manga from Yukichi-kun.

00:15:23.700 --> 00:15:24.840
You see?

00:15:24.840 --> 00:15:30.200
So I wanted to show you that there's 
something like this here, too.

00:15:33.680 --> 00:15:36.730
Wow! It's the ocean!

00:15:44.580 --> 00:15:46.680
This place is amazing!

00:15:46.680 --> 00:15:48.590
I didn't know it was so close to the ocean!

00:15:48.910 --> 00:15:52.590
Oh, there are a lot of people, 
and they all look like tennis players!

00:15:52.960 --> 00:15:54.350
I think it's because, at night,

00:15:54.350 --> 00:15:57.600
the ocean looks the same whether 
you're in Kanagawa or Chiba...

00:15:57.600 --> 00:16:01.090
But coming here really calms me down.

00:16:01.090 --> 00:16:02.890
Yeah, I can see why!

00:16:03.340 --> 00:16:04.600
This is great!

00:16:05.310 --> 00:16:06.110
Isn't it?

00:16:11.930 --> 00:16:14.280
Whoa, it's cold!

00:16:14.280 --> 00:16:16.700
But it feels good!

00:16:18.150 --> 00:16:20.370
Hey, don't hurt yourself.

00:16:20.750 --> 00:16:22.500
I know.

00:16:26.060 --> 00:16:27.640
<i>The ocean at night...</i>

00:16:26.980 --> 00:16:30.380
Hey, don't come up here!

00:16:27.640 --> 00:16:29.330
<i>Nat-chan having fun...</i>

00:16:31.510 --> 00:16:36.140
<i>I-Is this... my chance to tell her how I feel?!</i>

00:16:36.360 --> 00:16:39.890
Instinct

00:16:36.360 --> 00:16:39.890
If that's what you think, then spit it out! Go!

00:16:40.030 --> 00:16:47.650
Reason

00:16:40.220 --> 00:16:45.240
No, no, no! Something that important 
needs to be planned ahead!

00:16:45.240 --> 00:16:47.650
Besides, it's the day before your match!

00:16:47.650 --> 00:16:50.480
It's not a matter of when you should say it!

00:16:50.480 --> 00:16:55.890
No, no! Nat-chan invited me 
out here to help me relax!

00:16:55.890 --> 00:16:57.130
Okay, I'll ask you this.

00:16:57.130 --> 00:17:01.240
If I lose the Kanto tournament 
and only Nat-chan goes pro,

00:17:01.240 --> 00:17:04.390
can you say with conviction that 
you won't regret confessing today?

00:17:05.210 --> 00:17:06.200
Ei-chan?

00:17:06.770 --> 00:17:07.670
Ei-chan!

00:17:09.070 --> 00:17:11.840
What's wrong, Ei-chan? You look so serious.

00:17:11.840 --> 00:17:13.170
Oh, just...

00:17:24.440 --> 00:17:27.610
Um... Nat-chan...

00:17:39.430 --> 00:17:40.960
Thanks for always being there.

00:17:41.300 --> 00:17:44.200
What? Where's this coming 
from all of a sudden?

00:17:44.600 --> 00:17:46.030
It's not sudden.

00:17:46.030 --> 00:17:48.760
I feel like you're always helping me out.

00:17:49.260 --> 00:17:53.980
When I lost matches, when I went 
to Florida, and even right now.

00:17:56.230 --> 00:17:58.970
It's embarrassing when you 
come out and say it like that.

00:17:59.300 --> 00:18:01.970
I want to do something for you, too.

00:18:02.360 --> 00:18:04.710
So if you need anything, tell me, okay?

00:18:04.710 --> 00:18:07.290
If you need a hitting partner, 
I'll do it anytime.

00:18:07.290 --> 00:18:09.480
Oh, I think I'd appreciate that.

00:18:10.420 --> 00:18:11.380
Okay, then...

00:18:11.900 --> 00:18:13.500
Go out with me.

00:18:14.200 --> 00:18:16.400
If that's all, of course I...

00:18:17.080 --> 00:18:17.990
Huh?

00:18:18.070 --> 00:18:18.990
Huh?!

00:18:18.990 --> 00:18:21.750
What?! G-Go out?!

00:18:21.750 --> 00:18:23.410
U-Um, you mean...

00:18:23.410 --> 00:18:26.410
Wh-What?! Wh-Why?! You just... You're kidding!

00:18:26.410 --> 00:18:28.000
I'm not kidding.

00:18:31.210 --> 00:18:33.510
Then... you mean it?

00:18:33.960 --> 00:18:34.710
Yep.

00:18:40.180 --> 00:18:42.010
She beat me to it.

00:18:42.010 --> 00:18:43.010
Huh?

00:18:43.010 --> 00:18:47.330
I mean, all this time, I'd planned to say it first.

00:18:47.330 --> 00:18:50.080
What does it matter who says it first?

00:18:50.080 --> 00:18:53.020
B-But I was thinking of saying it all that time!

00:18:53.020 --> 00:18:55.020
And before, you said I was "cheating"...

00:18:55.020 --> 00:18:56.640
So I thought, this time...

00:18:56.640 --> 00:19:00.690
That was because you were asking about 
my feelings without telling me your own.

00:19:00.690 --> 00:19:02.820
Then why is it okay now?

00:19:02.820 --> 00:19:06.030
Because you told me how 
you felt not long ago.

00:19:06.030 --> 00:19:07.960
Even if you only got the "li—" out.

00:19:07.960 --> 00:19:12.220
Y-Yeah, but... I didn't get any further than "li."

00:19:12.220 --> 00:19:13.910
But I understood it.

00:19:13.910 --> 00:19:16.300
What do words matter, 
as long as the point gets across?

00:19:16.560 --> 00:19:18.800
I want to say it properly!

00:19:19.090 --> 00:19:22.300
Okay... Then say it again.

00:19:22.640 --> 00:19:24.100
Huh? Oh...

00:19:33.480 --> 00:19:37.430
I like you! Please go out with me!

00:19:37.430 --> 00:19:39.240
Okay, I will.

00:19:44.330 --> 00:19:46.440
Hey! Why are you laughing?

00:19:47.100 --> 00:19:48.170
Because...

00:19:49.980 --> 00:19:52.650
Hey, did you know it's already 9:00?

00:19:52.650 --> 00:19:55.240
Huh? It's already that late?

00:19:55.240 --> 00:19:59.780
But this was a lot better than stressing 
out over your notes, wasn't it?

00:19:59.780 --> 00:20:02.590
Huh? Oh, yeah.

00:20:03.460 --> 00:20:04.930
Hey, Ei-chan...

00:20:04.930 --> 00:20:06.260
What?

00:20:06.260 --> 00:20:09.370
I want to thank you, too.

00:20:09.370 --> 00:20:10.100
Huh?

00:20:10.420 --> 00:20:14.660
When you were practicing with Takuma 
before, and even before that...

00:20:15.240 --> 00:20:18.480
Ever since I first met you,

00:20:18.480 --> 00:20:23.360
seeing you work hard has always
made me want to work hard, too.

00:20:23.940 --> 00:20:26.920
Even when I've got it rough, 
I can tell myself to overcome it.

00:20:28.580 --> 00:20:32.890
So when you win, I'm as happy as if I had won,

00:20:32.890 --> 00:20:35.380
and that always gives me strength!

00:20:40.330 --> 00:20:41.380
<i>I feel like...</i>

00:20:42.700 --> 00:20:43.840
<i>I might cry.</i>

00:20:54.390 --> 00:20:56.280
Well, I'll see you tomorrow.

00:20:56.280 --> 00:20:56.900
Yeah.

00:20:57.130 --> 00:20:58.510
Let's both do our best!

00:20:58.510 --> 00:20:59.400
Yep!

00:21:01.400 --> 00:21:03.140
Welcome back, Bro.

00:21:03.140 --> 00:21:04.800
You were gone a while.

00:21:04.800 --> 00:21:07.800
Yeah... I went for a walk 
and ended up at the beach.

00:21:07.800 --> 00:21:09.400
The beach, huh?

00:21:09.400 --> 00:21:11.410
If we win tomorrow, want to light fireworks?

00:21:11.900 --> 00:21:12.910
Sounds good!

00:21:17.830 --> 00:21:21.090
<i>I never expected this to happen 
the day before my match.</i>

00:21:22.010 --> 00:21:24.580
<i>Life never goes the way you'd expect.</i>

00:21:26.640 --> 00:21:29.690
<i>All right! I'll do my best tomorrow!</i>

00:21:35.090 --> 00:21:36.690
Morning, Ei-chan.

00:21:36.690 --> 00:21:39.190
Oh... Morning!

00:21:39.510 --> 00:21:41.190
I'm digging in!

00:21:41.560 --> 00:21:43.850
This miso soup is good, isn't it?

00:21:43.850 --> 00:21:46.520
Y-Yeah. It is good.

00:21:49.730 --> 00:21:52.350
I-I think I'll go get seconds!

00:21:52.350 --> 00:21:54.900
It's unusual for you to get seconds.

00:21:54.900 --> 00:21:56.660
Huh? Oh...

00:22:00.760 --> 00:22:02.020
<i>They're acting weird.</i>

00:22:05.210 --> 00:22:07.970
Wow, look at all these people!

00:22:08.490 --> 00:22:14.220
Well, all the representatives of each age 
group from seven prefectures are here.

00:22:14.930 --> 00:22:17.980
But that number will be cut in half today.

00:22:19.020 --> 00:22:20.030
Half...

00:22:20.030 --> 00:22:20.870
Yeah.

00:22:22.050 --> 00:22:22.980
Listen up!

00:22:22.980 --> 00:22:25.970
All the STC players will survive to the end!

00:22:25.970 --> 00:22:26.990
Right!

00:22:27.600 --> 00:22:28.510
<i>Okay!</i>

00:22:29.940 --> 00:22:30.820
<i>Let's do this!</i>

00:24:00.000 --> 00:24:25.020
Next Time

00:24:00.570 --> 00:24:02.830
All right! I'm ready!

00:24:02.830 --> 00:24:04.290
Five minutes until we start!

00:24:04.290 --> 00:24:05.080
Here I go!

00:24:05.080 --> 00:24:06.090
Ei-chan! Ei-chan!

00:24:06.300 --> 00:24:07.460
Kageyama?

00:24:07.460 --> 00:24:10.070
What's wrong? My match is about to start.

00:24:10.070 --> 00:24:13.180
There's some big trouble with your next match!

00:24:13.180 --> 00:24:13.630
Huh?

00:24:13.630 --> 00:24:15.550
Your opponent isn't here yet!

00:24:15.760 --> 00:24:18.390
They say there was a traffic accident 
near where he was warming up!

00:24:18.390 --> 00:24:20.040
What?! No way!

00:24:20.730 --> 00:24:22.560
Next time on <i>Baby Steps</i>,

00:24:21.540 --> 00:24:25.020
A Hero and Loud Cheers

00:24:22.560 --> 00:24:24.230
"A Hero and Loud Cheers."

00:24:25.210 --> 00:24:31.000
End
